nd the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{7}=2\\sqrt{7}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ab7bfc4-fe0b-5271-b8ca-448cc2f51cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247805} {:answer/id #uuid "515c4642-4ca5-5554-a9a2-a99042231e23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$5$ and $2.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248154} {:answer/id #uuid "5390bb0d-24f6-53b5-94f1-003ff942f21a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$50$ and $12.5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248176} {:answer/id #uuid "7c004586-c7f0-5ef1-b7fc-ca0dc8582a7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$100$ and $25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248512} {:answer/id #uuid "f6dfbabe-5660-549f-96d1-e202fb8340ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$10$ and $5$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ab7bfc4-fe0b-5271-b8ca-448cc2f51cca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$20$ and $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247805} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ac28089-ed40-5056-81d0-446e067aefea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249880}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41a42db1-4c6e-506f-8c7d-8db6141e0014" :question/math-academy-id "q-115135" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{100}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=100$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=100,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{100}=10.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=10,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 10=20,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284503 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d9bb51-7d28-5203-a100-671bfb7b1984" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281995} {:answer/id #uuid "a39c00a4-afcb-520f-b854-4bc1d26a2c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283115} {:answer/id #uuid "b2234da2-6880-5948-bede-cdef269e6b98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $4$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283232} {:answer/id #uuid "cbccc52e-55e7-5e83-85bf-7ec1fde391a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283470} {:answer/id #uuid "fe3590a4-fe8c-559b-a199-73736d3c5178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283921}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a39c00a4-afcb-520f-b854-4bc1d26a2c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2\\sqrt{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283115} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a67a626-3555-5355-acc5-d65f47afb3ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc47bd40-4608-5f54-a026-2eadf6dc5b59" :question/math-academy-id "q-16452" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=2.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=2,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=2,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284508 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ea4dfa-3746-512d-a4e5-fa19281f7cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281707} {:answer/id #uuid "119639f4-439c-5028-9a09-08e66ef5732b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281856} {:answer/id #uuid "376b6ab6-79ed-53f0-aaa3-87bd75aa6c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282182} {:answer/id #uuid "66196dd8-4f71-57e1-8517-24340f5f07aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282569} {:answer/id #uuid "95c0623c-a78b-5fec-8c1e-678b85527dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66196dd8-4f71-57e1-8517-24340f5f07aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282569} :answer-field/id #uuid "29260e1c-0c08-5549-8699-d160c488888a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a341dec-953c-5c37-b7a1-a5cd95c6de7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-16454" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=12.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=12,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294936 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177cbba2-b79a-5f5d-9c48-f99cc18456dc" :an