as length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 8=16.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc25ece-e5e8-5341-b369-60c89d7b7cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc25ece-e5e8-5341-b369-60c89d7b7cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293391} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5ea0c3-f3db-587a-a55c-d246902036fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8edd52d8-a856-5699-9135-823330f651e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8edd52d8-a856-5699-9135-823330f651e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293486} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a02e34-a1c4-5302-b6ca-ab014cebd574" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294782}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26bde4a4-e1ca-5778-ae0f-4fa44e3f19d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279165" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=4.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=4,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=3,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295048 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c243753-ebfb-5bd5-b708-979771972883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c243753-ebfb-5bd5-b708-979771972883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293476} :answer-field/id #uuid "2813c84a-d103-5cb1-bd59-405c9d238f89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e23f6045-b753-590b-95e0-5f04f82ba4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e23f6045-b753-590b-95e0-5f04f82ba4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293819} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f5d06e6-62e7-51fd-886c-846c8398c0d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05eafcf1-2e1f-53c8-892c-751fcabef6c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279166" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee64a24f-4e3c-5796-94b8-769faa4d203e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee64a24f-4e3c-5796-94b8-769faa4d203e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293859} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d433ad7-9ca0-5240-8e86-ff3b484b7323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294199} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1efda85-532c-5456-9085-146b731f4efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1efda85-532c-5456-9085-146b731f4efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293689} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9daf9a-554c-59f2-8703-ec452d9cbcc0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c976c0d3-2975-5e8a-a067-1b42fba6644e" :question/math-academy-id "q-279169" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=4$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=4,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=5,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd07ce69-7233-50e2-ade0-35bd41ecc948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293668}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd07ce69-7233-50e2-ade0-35bd41ecc948" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293668} :answer-field/id #uuid "3506445f-e25d-5eed-9620-502f0