e $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186401537 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "755a881c-6b14-5e96-bd68-6af58d5ef813" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$8$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401539} {:answer/id #uuid "5965e390-56a0-55ef-a7dc-eff34c09cc53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401540} {:answer/id #uuid "1f629da2-c549-5180-8903-3a78b8767616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401541} {:answer/id #uuid "1c1fc5c2-bdfa-52e9-a59e-c6227d171448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401542} {:answer/id #uuid "47a16fa9-9d49-55d0-a143-c2b6cca5c4dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f629da2-c549-5180-8903-3a78b8767616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{2}$ and $2$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401541} :answer-field/id #uuid "b41dd28d-0ca0-5222-9cfe-700ddaa37f17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186401538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e791f5b6-5e18-534a-99e5-45cc16c1809f" :question/math-academy-id "q-16455" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{1}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{8}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=1$ and ${b}^{2}=8.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=1,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{1}=1.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=8,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=1.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2}=4\\sqrt{2},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 1=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434277 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434263}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1dcd62ed-d1d5-5d66-b9a7-d3752b72ffcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434263} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f59ee40-6a49-5f76-9b09-b56f1e7b8c65" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434274} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cb3f03d-cfef-5f9f-b396-26b221d4f856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434266} :answer-field/id #uuid "62dc0b83-a470-59d2-b62b-b5ccbaa907c1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c46acbe-8af8-5805-a582-9ade9300c9a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-279199" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{13}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=13$ and ${b}^{2}=36.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=13,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{13}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=36,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{13}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{13}=2\\sqrt{13}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186434279 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb06d992-e82f-5977-a714-2f2fd87616b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434271}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb06d992-e82f-5977-a714-2f2fd87616b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434271} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f8d6b7-9861-51ad-96d2-5cd3b96789b2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434272} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56513915-f193-5d63-936d-07a8b133ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "56513915-f193-5d63-936d-07a8b133ceae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434268} :answer-field/id #uuid "878be2a7-5abd-5dc4-9fe0-30ce370e3435" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186434276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb8398f9-e97a-58eb-bd8b-b49ccd2d689d" :question/math-academy-id "q-279167" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=49$ and ${b}^{2}=25.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=49,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{49}=7.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25}=5.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=7,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 7=14,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 5=10.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "317cc575-d6d9-5bf7-b402-e9f6f2aece5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543849} {:answer/id #uuid "37d68e3d-f8d6-5f13-a869-d9cdc65b796c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543852} {:answer/id #uuid "7693e799-17b4-580e-85ba-48cd63b488fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543867} {:answer/id #uuid "e77191fb-4308-5ae9-92dc-890558829810" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{5}{4}$ and $\\frac{2}{9}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543899} {:answer/id #uuid "f6547e1e-09da-5e3a-9109-8fd09fcf5409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543901}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "317cc575-d6d9-5bf7-b402-e9f6f2aece5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543849} :answer-field/id #uuid "6254bf33-2529-515f-a80a-8ecdfac48523" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543860}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "071541e3-e659-523c-b1f4-eade008267f7" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{5}{4}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{2}{9}}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{4}$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{2}{9}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{4},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{2}{9},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543853 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce4db2e6-57cc-53c9-a74c-1ffe1f592efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce4db2e6-57cc-53c9-a74c-1ffe1f592efd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{70}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543890} :answer-field/id #uuid "9736611d-7a2c-5da0-acc9-2bf3c1d58488" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbc2dfdf-cb86-5fc6-aae5-463332bc08d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{82}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbc2dfdf-cb86-5fc6-aae5-463332bc08d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{82}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543885} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6df07a4-3e4e-56fb-903b-6dca2e87c255" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a6ef55b-f35c-5e25-8e8b-c766bf7961eb" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{82}{9}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{70}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{82}{9}$ and ${b}^{2}=70.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{82}{9},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{82}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=70,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{70}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{70},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{70}=2\\sqrt{70},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{82}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{82}}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543855 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf7d248d-e685-5e26-ac25-a7926e2cbb3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf7d248d-e685-5e26-ac25-a7926e2cbb3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543891} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa5ddd2d-b3d6-55bf-8001-4f05c1087233" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae9ca8da-f70b-516d-94a6-97e74c60595b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543881}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae9ca8da-f70b-516d-94a6-97e74c60595b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543881} :answer-field/id #uuid "f905f086-bf87-543a-a849-4cd7d74a502f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543904}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3f4b4f77-3a6a-59e9-8972-8eb1480893b3" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{27}{4}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{3}{16}}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{27}{4}$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{3}{16}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{27}{4},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{4}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{3}{16},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{16}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}=3\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543858 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{: