^{2}=\\frac{5}{9}$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{5}{16}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{9},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{5}{16},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{16}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{4}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543859 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15738b3d-a199-50b9-9fa5-42bf040af44b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543845} {:answer/id #uuid "7639f7e6-85b3-522f-bf24-1e51f41a7916" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543866} {:answer/id #uuid "84ba063b-79d0-5f5c-bf77-db44f8a5f850" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543871} {:answer/id #uuid "f0cc75ef-eeea-50c8-9c25-52c64d9dd650" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\frac{3}{4}$ and $\\frac{5}{9}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543900} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e25a61-f7f8-5151-9dad-062a3e7efa79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7e25a61-f7f8-5151-9dad-062a3e7efa79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543903} :answer-field/id #uuid "96cd1554-de00-552f-a26b-2763f1e070c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543875}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5cca8aca-b32e-5ccf-8a3f-4520b45e3d49" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{5}{9}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{3}{4}}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{9}$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{9},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{3}{4},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543869 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c58d987-961a-585e-a491-00bbed01b89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c58d987-961a-585e-a491-00bbed01b89a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543862} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f76cdf7-8c2e-5196-9f1e-b93f95d0b0e2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543847} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29710f27-4a0c-540d-9afb-36c328129c2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543848}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29710f27-4a0c-540d-9afb-36c328129c2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543848} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5baf09d-53ca-5d62-bb06-c003ce6dd6fc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "81fb6273-5dee-5beb-bfc9-3f4b77ae324c" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{5}{4}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{27}{4}}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{4}$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{27}{4}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{5}{4},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{5}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{27}{4},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{27}{4}}=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}=3\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}=\\sqrt{5}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543878 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e7a2f97-cecf-54f4-977c-ad480185865c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$37$ and $\\frac{73}{9}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543863} {:answer/id #uuid "82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543870} {:answer/id #uuid "b3598dd1-c765-5f19-9a18-ce18efdacfdc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543883} {:answer/id #uuid "cb386ed9-a60a-507f-a0a0-3b956d0d46eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543889} {:answer/id #uuid "d4ab06df-aa62-554d-b1a3-91a2d87f977e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82e1672b-a1cf-5e4f-b7ec-400e71ee5eb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{37}$ and $\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543870} :answer-field/id #uuid "db39f157-86de-5b5e-aa65-9e3ecfdb909d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543897}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8e4213c-472e-5df6-a92b-8b65321f34cc" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{37}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{73}{9}}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=37$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{73}{9}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=37,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{37}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{73}{9},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{73}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=\\sqrt{37},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{37}=2\\sqrt{37},$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{73}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{73}}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543886 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0005c1d8-45ea-525d-a5f3-270652f70c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543843} {:answer/id #uuid "346354a8-96ab-5ac3-afa2-7e1332833460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543850} {:answer/id #uuid "3b9750c6-a897-50af-bf8f-f7809c90a66d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$53$ and $\\frac{13}{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543854} {:answer/id #uuid "40f0a89a-ba5c-5eb5-a4c7-9438df455d0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543856} {:answer/id #uuid "a21ae6c2-3d2e-5bd5-bda8-5f05bc8b8bc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{53}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186