uid "ac8378fb-e823-5792-b0e8-141ffa012178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{47}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543880} :answer-field/id #uuid "50ac688e-f2ed-5c1e-b30b-f87af88a4c4e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543857} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4f06786-52b2-5301-9c27-c84a9739b589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4f06786-52b2-5301-9c27-c84a9739b589" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543887} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c7c7107-1beb-5ce0-af4d-c6cb96a01e5b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543873}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d560ab9f-5f69-5c94-a9a1-63ff925308ba" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{\\frac{47}{9}}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=16$ and ${b}^{2}=\\frac{47}{9}.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=16,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=\\frac{47}{9},$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{\\frac{47}{9}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{47}}{3}.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=4,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=\\frac{\\sqrt{47}}{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 4=8,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{47}}{3}=\\frac{2\\sqrt{47}}{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186543898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6418b296-10d2-5b35-b945-05b31aba2d9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543861} {:answer/id #uuid "90328bb5-2efb-5b62-9495-b0a760fef10a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$17$ and $\\frac{13}{4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543874} {:answer/id #uuid "d3bb7b1f-836e-5b98-9cdd-890c7f95b0ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543892} {:answer/id #uuid "d502494b-1775-539d-9e06-67be767210e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543895} {:answer/id #uuid "f7023301-1a20-54bd-92af-1b064d386811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543902}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7023301-1a20-54bd-92af-1b064d386811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{17}$ and $\\sqrt{13}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543902} :answer-field/id #uuid "7347b547-af23-57b6-bf2a-d08e54524091" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186543864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e487ead8-2208-53bd-a890-504c42fca111" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\frac{13}{4}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{17}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=\\frac{13}{4}$ and ${b}^{2}=17.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=\\frac{13}{4},$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{\\frac{13}{4}}=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=17,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{17}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=\\sqrt{17},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{17}=2\\sqrt{17},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{2}=\\sqrt{13}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Lengths of the Major and Minor Axes Given the Equation of an Ellipse"}]}
